{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The memory card fits my repeated need for removable storage, provided my devices support its capacity.",
    "The USB extension would make my card reader easier to reach, and the longer HDMI cable could help connect compatible equipment to my existing TV. Both support equipment I already use."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo speakers introduce a voice assistant I have not shown a need for; owning a Fire tablet does not make that a natural next purchase for me.",
    "Another tablet, a surveillance kit, and streaming equipment each require a new need that my purchases do not establish. My camera accessories support photography, not necessarily home security.",
    "The large speaker-wire pack assumes a wiring project, while my cable purchases have addressed specific connections."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire 7 purchase seems to have been treated as interest in a wider range of Amazon devices, although I mainly bought accessories to use with it.",
    "My interest in cameras and electronics seems to have been stretched into interest in surveillance and smart-home equipment without a clear connection to what I need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I repeatedly buy practical accessories for existing equipment, including storage, adapters, cables, mounts, and protective items. The specific job an accessory solves matters to me.",
    "Compatibility matters: memory capacity support, connector type, and fit determine whether something is useful. A related product name alone is not enough.",
    "Frequent accessory purchases do not mean I need to replace my tablet or start a new speaker, streaming, or security setup."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my need for storage and connections, but inferred too much interest in new devices from purchases supporting equipment I already own."
}"}
